From: Banana <bananalinux@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gfx/widgets: leave out the load-content animation

RetroArch's loading animation is drawn by the widget layer, which (unlike the
menu texture and the game) is not turned with the panel on KMS/GBM. On a handheld
whose panel is mounted turned in the shell it therefore reads sideways for the
moment a game starts. Leave it out: banana-ui already owns the boot animation,
and a sideways splash is worse than none.

Upstream-Status: Not applicable
---
--- a/gfx/gfx_widgets.c
+++ b/gfx/gfx_widgets.c
@@ -63,8 +63,11 @@
 #endif
    &gfx_widget_generic_message,
    &gfx_widget_libretro_message,
-   &gfx_widget_progress_message,
-   &gfx_widget_load_content_animation
+   &gfx_widget_progress_message
+   /* &gfx_widget_load_content_animation: banana-ui's boot animation is the one
+    * the user sees; RetroArch's loading animation is drawn by its widget layer,
+    * which is not turned with the panel on KMS/GBM, so it reads sideways for the
+    * moment a game starts. Left out rather than shown wrong. */
 };
 
 #if defined(HAVE_MENU) && defined(HAVE_XMB)
